id=a52sxq_mediaprovider_leveldb_stale
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: MediaProvider backup works again on phones updated without a wipe
author=kusti420
description=Diagnosed 2026-10-24: phones updated without a wipe across the S26U base switch (2026-10-10) run MediaProvider (com.google.android.providers.media.module) under a new app uid (e.g. 10274), but its LevelDB backup dirs /data/media/<user>/.transforms/recovery/leveldb-{internal,external_primary,ownership,<volume id>} still belong to the old uid (10293, categories c37), mode 2750. FuseDaemon's DB::Open fails ("LOCK: Permission denied"), so every boot logs "Leveldb setup is missing" and every media change "Missing leveldb connection", and MediaProvider's database backup/recovery stays off. Deleting the stale dirs by hand and rebooting fixed it on the test phone (MediaProvider recreated them, "Leveldb connection established"). Fix: k4-leveldb-stale, started by init when user 0's credential-encrypted storage unlocks (before StorageManager mounts emulated;0 and FuseDaemon opens the backup) (service k4_leveldb_stale, user 0 only) and at boot completed for every other user (k4_leveldb_stale_late: sys.user.N.ce_available exists only for user 0, and Secure Folder unlocks ~8 s after boot completed on the test phone, so it waits up to 2 min for a locked user; MediaProvider of that user picks the dirs up at its next start at the latest), removes exactly those dirs: a leveldb-* dir under .transforms/recovery of a numeric user, real directory (no symlink anywhere on the way, physical path re-checked), labelled media_rw_data_file, owned by an app uid of that user other than the current MediaProvider uid from packages.list, holding only LevelDB files; files are unlinked from inside the dir after re-checking its inode and owner, then rmdir (never rm -r). Everything else is left alone and only a mismatch is logged (kmsg, "k4-leveldb-stale:"); a clean phone and a fresh install do nothing. Own SELinux domain k4leveldb: read packages.list, list /data/media, unlink files and rmdir dirs of type media_rw_data_file, nothing else; root with CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE only.
